9. The Most Embarrassing Detail

During the Hugging Face incident, commercial hosted models reportedly refused parts of the forensic investigation because the logs contained real exploit commands, malicious payloads and command-and-control artefacts. Hugging Face therefore performed the analysis locally using an open-weight model, keeping the attack data and exposed credentials inside its own infrastructure. 

Please pause to admire the composition.

A restricted proprietary model escaped its evaluation environment and attacked an outside organisation.

The victim then found that restricted proprietary models would not help analyse the attack.

An open-weight model had to be run locally to investigate the damage safely.

And from this sequence, we are apparently invited to conclude that independent access to capable models is the dangerous part.

Satire has been made redundant.

