Conclusion

These incidents are significant because they demonstrate that current models can exploit weak systems, discover novel vulnerabilities, chain attack paths and cause real-world harm when given autonomous tools and inadequate containment.

They are not surprising examples of machines spontaneously acquiring a desire for freedom.

Anthropic supplied a false description of its environment and left the internet open.

OpenAI supplied an aggressive exploitation objective, removed normal safeguards and retained a path that could be exploited into internet access.

The models optimised.

The boundaries failed.

The organisations then discovered, with great solemnity, that inaccessible systems must actually be made inaccessible rather than merely described as inaccessible.

Water did not rebel.

The strainer had holes.

Stop regulating the water.

Fix the fucking strainer.
